## Objective
- Act as an autonomous bug-bounty agent per `skills/AGENT.md`, testing all 85 top-level routes of `https://console.byteplus.com` (from `data/targets.txt`) for client-side then server-side vulnerabilities, and record only confirmed, reproducible high-impact findings in `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`; cwd same.
- Must read `skills/AGENT.md` fully at session start (single source of truth); also `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`. No user questions — self-answer and act.
- Scope: `data/targets.txt` URL list only (85 `https://console.byteplus.com/...` routes) + same-origin JS/API required to exercise them. No sibling domains, subdomains, third parties, CDNs as test targets. Out-of-scope items go to `result/out-of-scope.txt`. Missing/ambiguous scope → `result/BLOCKED.md`.
- Main priorities: client-side attacker-source→sink with impact; server-side mass assignment on create/edit/update endpoints and parameter guessing. Use test-owned data; no `200`/reflected-string/accepted-field claims without runtime proof.
- Creds (`creds/test-account.txt`, intentionally public/disposable):
  - A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566`
  - B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345`
  - Login URL: `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/`
- Session: logged in as `test-user-123`, AccountID `3000823185`.
- Resume state: `decision=preserved`; target hash `b5e187557fbf8e0f90e933fdd2595b20ef4600b6c02ef29a3723a2187b77f8d5`; prior run watchdog-terminated with only `result/scope.md`, no findings/inventory.
- Session start (UTC): `2026-10-29T06:25:00Z`; ~5h35m testing window, hard job timeout 5h55m.
- Environment: GitHub Actions linux; Chrome 156 headless at `http://127.0.0.1:9222`; chrome-devtools MCP works (1 page target).
- Tools present: `opencode`, `curl`, `git`, `node v22.23.4`, `npx`, `python3`, `google-chrome-stable`. **`rg` is NOT installed** — use Python/grep.
- Constraints observed: only navigate/visit (no destructive clicks); avoid creating billable cloud resources.

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight: dirs exist (`creds/`, `data/`, `skills/`, `result/{client-side,findings,inventory,logs}`, `tools/`, `vulnebleti/`); chrome devtools `/json/version` OK.
- Read `skills/AGENT.md` (truncated), `client-side-skill.md`, `server-side-skill.md`; read `data/targets.txt`, `creds/README.md`, `creds/test-account.txt`, `result/scope.md`, `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`, `result/logs/session.md`, `result/logs/target-state.txt`, `result/logs/targets.sha256`.
- Wrote session metadata to `result/logs/session.md`; saved login headers to `result/logs/login-headers.txt`.
- Logged in via Chrome DevTools MCP with account A → redirected to `/home` as `test-user-123` (no captcha encountered).
- Built `tools/cdp.mjs` (raw CDP over Node WebSocket): commands `cookies`, `eval '<js>'`, `get <url> [outfile]`.
- Extracted all cookies to `/tmp/cookies.json`; built cookie header `/tmp/cookiehdr.txt` (2611 bytes).
- Fetched all 85 route HTMLs with curl + cookies → `/tmp/bp/pages/*.html`, all HTTP 200 (`/tmp/bp/fetch_res.txt`).
- Parsed initial HTML: 739 unique JS URLs → `/tmp/bp/js_urls.txt`, `/tmp/bp/byroute.json`; downloaded to `/tmp/bp/js` (hashed filenames, 316MB).
- Built `tools/crawl.mjs` (CDP crawler: `Network.enable`, `Page.navigate`, waits 4500ms, records scripts/XHR/fetch + final URL). Ran all 85 routes → `/tmp/bp/crawl.json`, log `/tmp/bp/crawl.log`.
  - Results: 2324 unique scripts, 276 unique API URLs → `/tmp/bp/crawl_scripts.txt`, `/tmp/bp/crawl_api.txt`; many routes redirect to sub-routes (e.g. `/dts/region:dts+ap-southeast-1/?`, `/datarangers/org/2100230837/app/list`, `/user/basics/`).
- Downloaded 1478 additional `res.gcloudcache.com` bundles → `/tmp/bp/js` now 738MB / 2217 files.
- Static analysis outputs (all in `/tmp/bp/`):
  - `loc_candidates.txt` (864 lines), `decode_loc.txt` (221), `param_nav.txt` (95)
  - `source_sink.txt` (1001), `scan_sink.txt` (344), `msgscan.txt` (643), `msg_app.txt` (208)
- Key negative results: no `location.href=decodeURIComponent(...)` or `location.assign/replace(decodeURIComponent(...))` in downloaded bundles; most `innerHTML`/`document.write` hits are echarts/libraries; most postMessage listeners are polyfill/axios noise.
- Navigated to `https://console.byteplus.com/user` → `/user/basics/`; listed 111 network requests via `chrome-devtools_list_network_requests`.
- Found user-mono bundle URL `https://res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/console-user-mono/byteplus/static/js/1.0.0.2492/main.4ec0f485.js` → local `/tmp/bp/js/68e2d2c26ed70c02.js` (1,750,329 bytes).
- Enumerated account API paths from bundles, incl. `/api/top/account_verify/ap-southeast-1/2018-01-01/{CompleteProfile,UpdateProfile,GetProfileStatus,SendProfileSMSCaptcha,SendProfileVoiceCaptcha,CreateGoChinaApplication}`, `/api/top/account_management/ap-southeast-1/2018-01-01/SendCodeForBindAccountSecurityPhone`, `/api/auth/user/unified_settings`, `/api/common/passport/getUser`, `/api/passport/account/getUser`, `/api/passport/security/encCerts`.

### Active
- Investigating server-side account/profile surface via `console-user-mono` bundle (`main.4ec0f485.js`); enumerating all `Update*/Modify*/Set*` action names and their parameter schemas for mass-assignment candidates.
- Candidate client-side leads pending validation:
  - `vconsole-auth/byteplus/static/js/1.0.0.2811/main.adbc4e5a.js`: `N=()=>_.parse(location.search).redirectURI`; `redirectURI` passed as `redir_uri` to login request (server-side redirect) — possible open redirect; test `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=https://example.com/` in a fresh browser context.
  - `bp-cdn-main` reads `accountId`, `userId`, `token` from URL → sessionStorage/localStorage → uses `x-jwt-token` / `TopAccountId` headers (possible mirror/account-switch feature; needs a valid token to exploit).
  - `byteplus-faas` `main.edc16495.js` postMessage listener with no origin check (checks `window.self!==window.top`; typed handler dispatch) — needs handler analysis for sensitive actions.
  - `ml-platform` codespace `innerHTML` is a static string — **not** exploitable.

### Blocked
- `rg` unavailable (`/bin/bash: rg: command not found`) — scans use Python/grep.
- 738MB of JS creates heavy noise; library code dominates sink matches.
- No confirmed vulnerability yet; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` still header-only.
- Testing write/create endpoints carries cost/side-effect risk; avoid billable resource creation.

## Next Move
1. In `/tmp/bp/js/68e2d2c26ed70c02.js` (user-mono main), extract all `Update*`/`Modify*`/`Set*`/`Create*` action names + request field names and map them to `/api/top/...` paths to identify mass-assignment candidates.
2. Capture full request/response bodies+headers for account-management APIs (extend `tools/cdp.mjs`/`tools/crawl.mjs` or use `chrome-devtools_get_network_request`) then replay with extra fields via curl using `/tmp/cookiehdr.txt` to test mass assignment/IDOR.
3. Test `redirectURI` open-redirect in an isolated Chrome context with account A login.
4. If no client-side win emerges, systematically test high-value routes (`/iam`, `/organization`, `/cloudidentity`, `/finance`, `/message`, `/workorder`, `/resourcemanager`, `/config`, `/cloudtrail`) using captured API endpoints in `crawl_api.txt`.

