## Objective
- Act as an autonomous bug-bounty agent per `skills/AGENT.md`: find valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities in in-scope assets only, prove with practical evidence, and report under `result/`.
- In-scope target: `https://console.byteplus.com/` route list from `data/targets.txt` (86 top-level routes).

## Important Details
- Workflow: read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`; test one route at a time; no duplicate testing; practical evidence only; no CAPTCHA bypass; if access unavailable mark Unresolved.
- Scope is `console.byteplus.com` only. `res.gcloudcache.com` is a third-party CDN — out of scope as a document origin, but its bundles are loaded into in-scope console routes.
- Resume state: `target_hash=b5e187557fbf8e0f90e933fdd2595b20ef4600b6c02ef29a3723a2187b77f8d5`, decision=preserved (unchanged across runs).
- Prior work: 85 routes crawled, 278 unique API endpoints, exactly 2 client-side reports before this session (`/datarangers`, `/datatester`), `/dts` route-report. Prior ledger: 18+ server-side tests, no confirmed findings.
- Creds: account A `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` → AccountID 3000823185 (`test-user-123`); account B `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` → AccountID 3001021825 (`attacker-org`).
- Watchdogs kill opus after ~120s of no log output; checkpoint frequently. Current run 40848789625 started ~09:20Z, hard window ~14:10Z.
- All top-level routes return HTTP 302 unauthenticated (curl confirmed). No persisted session cookies from prior runs (`result/logs/login-headers.txt` only has `csrfToken`, `__spti`, `__sptiho`).

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight done: repo structure, targets, creds, prior inventory/ledger/logs reviewed; MCP Chrome available (Chrome/156.0.8078.73, port 9222).
- `/message` client-side static pass: no source→HTML/exec sink; `readMessage` postMessage listener exact same-origin; debugger `devtool:web:ready` listener accepts any origin but low impact (no secret/DOM sink). Report written; `result/logs/client-side.log` appended; `result/testing-inventory.json` updated (`tested` flag + 2 JS entries; note schema uses `file`/`route` keys, not `url`).
- `/ark`: downloaded 7 bundles to `result/client-side/console.byteplus.com/ark/javascript/` (main.ac478a41e8.js, async-main.f0b90c71f0.js, 4271.bf2bd0cb16.js, etc.) with `sha256.txt`. Analysis: `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` all React-Router SSR internals/helmet (not attacker-controlled); no open redirect; postMessage listeners are TEA SDK debugger only → no finding (route-report not yet written).
- Login attempts (A and B) both hit drag-puzzle CAPTCHA; stopped per rules. Marked auth unavailable.
- Mined `result/logs/opencode.log` → 682 unique `res.gcloudcache.com/...*.js` URLs saved to `/tmp/opencode/jslist.txt`; downloaded to `/tmp/opencode/js_cache` (318M); scan script `/tmp/opencode/scan.py` output `/tmp/opencode/scan_out.txt` (245 hits mostly polyfill noise; 5 real sink-proximity hits).
- Session continuation notes appended to `result/logs/session.md`.

### Active
- Investigating postMessage→DOM XSS candidate in `https://res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/inf/cs/byteplus_storage_dbw/static/js/index.83bfed73.js` (local: `/tmp/opencode/js_cache/451_index.83bfed73.js`):
  - `MessageSDK` (extends EventTarget): `window.addEventListener("message", ...)` accepts when `event.origin===this.messageOrigin || this.messageOrigin==="*"`, parses string JSON, `isSDKMessageEventPayload(payload, this.receivePrefix)`, then `this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(miniType,{detail:{...payload.data,originEvent:event}}))`.
  - Client role created via `createMessageSDK2({messageOrigin:"*", role:"client", ...})`; client `receivePrefix = serverEventPrefix`, server `receivePrefix = clientEventPrefix`.
  - `this.addEventListener("inject_script", injectScript)`: `injectScript` appends `<script>` with `innerHTML = evalString` (or `src`); `injectStyle` sets `style.innerHTML = style`. => arbitrary JS if message `{type:"<serverPrefix>:inject_script", data:{evalString:"..."}}` reaches it.
  - Prefix strings seen: `bytecloud_2_volc_event` (server→client), `volc_2_bytecloud_event` (client→server).
  - Init gating: `quickInit()` only runs if `inBytecloudSimple` (jwt query param or sessionStorage `_bc_in_bytecloud`); `forceInit` always initializes and is exported as `YO`; `bytecloudClient` exported as `df`. Need to find `YO(`/`forceInit` callers.
  - Same pattern expected in `byteplus_storage_dms/ebs/kafka/nas/rabbitmq/tls/vepfs` bundles.
  - Open question: does this code execute in `console.byteplus.com` origin (loaded via `window.__VOLCF_APPS__` `staticFiles` into console document) — in scope — or inside an iframe at `res.gcloudcache.com` — out of scope? `index.html` for dbw is a "Cloud-CLI Template" with no script refs.

### Blocked
- Login blocked by drag-puzzle CAPTCHA on both root login and IAM-user login; cannot obtain authenticated session for runtime verification or server-side tests.
- No valid session cookies recoverable from prior logs.
- Runtime PoC for the postMessage candidate requires an in-scope authenticated page that loads the storage bundle.

